fast-docx-text is a reimplementation, in Rust, of the plain-text extraction of
mammoth (https://github.com/mwilliamson/mammoth.js): its document model's reading
of a .docx and its raw-text writer, which crates/fast-docx-text/src/raw_text.rs
follows element for element. It also reproduces how JSZip reads a zip archive and
how @xmldom/xmldom parses XML as mammoth drives them, and carries the dingbat table
of dingbat-to-unicode (crates/fast-docx-text/src/dingbats.rs, generated from that
package by scripts/generate-dingbats.mjs).

